==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{was wotd|2011|December|12}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|devil|devil's}} {{m|en|advocate}}, a {{calque|en|la|advocātus diabolī||the devil’s advocate|nocap=1}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[devil]]'s [[advocate]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} One who [[debate]]s from a viewpoint which he or she may not actually hold, usually to determine its [[validity]] or simply for the sake of [[argument]].
# {{qualifier|Roman Catholic Church}} A [[canon]] lawyer appointed by the [[Church]] to argue against the canonization of the proposed [[candidate]].

